{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown","id":487011,"title":"Raising Renown","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-20T21:22:28-07:00","id":487011,"title":"Raising Renown","content":"So I started a werewolf chronicle recently. I've run a lot of various splats before so I thought I was prepared for anything, lol. However, renown seems to be unique to the uratha. It is both a power source (makes you better the higher it is) and &quot;fame&quot; at the same time. And that's cool, I like it.<br /> <br /> My problem is that I have no idea how to deal with it. Two of my players have enough xp to buy up their renown (they're both going for Glory). And at first they were really excited, then they realized that they have to <i>do</i> things that would be &quot;glorious.&quot; So far nothing they've faced or done has really been super impressive (or maybe our outlook on what is impressive is too much?). So they decided they wanted to seek out something &quot;glorious&quot; to hunt. But then they realized that would completely sidetrack the chronicle's direction (as well as focus mostly on them). So there's a lot of mixed feelings. They want to spend their xp, not wait for a &quot;glorious fight,&quot; but they don't want to steal the game from the other players.<br /> <br /> I had imagined renown as being a sort of &quot;story reward&quot;. I.E. The storyteller could dole out situations to possibly increase various renown and then the players made use of those situations. But I can see their point, they earned the xp, and they want to spend it on raising their primary &quot;supernatural attribute&quot;. Or it might just be a failing on my part as I'm new to werewolf and not used to this yet. But I would love some advice on dealing with renown. Are we being too &quot;strict&quot; in our readings of the types of things to gain it? Should my players be more patient because renown is not a thing that should increase so often?<br /> <br /> One of my players offered the suggestion of perhaps just making renown not be an xp thing at all, but instead doled out <i>solely</i> by the storyteller.<br /> How do you all deal with renown?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T21:26:21-07:00","id":487033,"title":"","content":"Going to need more information than generalities to be able to answer any of those questions other than the last.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T21:39:22-07:00","id":487038,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Satchel. Especially since there's no way to tell what could sidetrack your chronicle without knowing what's happening in it. Glory can be gained for something as 'simple' as defeating a superior foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T21:57:42-07:00","id":487042,"title":"","content":"I mentioned this in the other thread, but in order to avoid this issue, I first find out what my players are interested in buying next, and then plan for that in the chronicle. So, two players tell me they both want to buy a dot of Glory. Cool. I know that Renown dots cost 3 experiences, and I know my players earn an average of 4 Beats per session. At that rate, they'll have enough to buy that dot of Glory in about 4 sessions. So, I plan an opportunity for them to do something Glorious, and prepare a 4 session questline culminating in that event. If they get up to 3 xp a little early, that's fine, they have a bit of a head start on what ever they want to pursue next. If they're still a few Beats short by the time they do the Glorious thing, that's fine too, I'll just note that they're a few Beats in debt.<br /> <br /> In general, my games are very player-directed. At the most basic level, they set the goals, and I put obstacles in the way of those goals. If possible, I try to do it in a way that poses dramatic questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T22:58:04-07:00","id":487060,"title":"","content":"I guess I expected more of a vague &quot;this is how I do it&quot; rather than responding exactly to what we have done so far. I'm not sure why, honestly.<br /> <br /> So our chronicle has been fairly short so far. And due to time constraints, what was supposed to be a single nights adventure became three nights/weeks of adventure.<br /> <br /> The pack has 6 uratha, one in each auspice, but two of the crescent moons (I haven't memorized all the names yet.)<br /> The chronicle began by paying/dealing with a spirit that lives on their territory. This has been set up as a prior arrangement, every month on the new moon, they gift this spirit with three essence and it crafts them a talen. Sort of a trade of mutual respect. This time, the spirit told them of some new misery spirits that had entered the area, and it didnt like them. The pack agreed to check it out.<br /> -In the area they found 8 misery spirits. 7 rank 1, and a single rank 2. The pack immediately attacked them, to clear them out. It was not a hard battle, there was little damage to the uratha and only a single one even took gauru form at all.<br /> -Once the spirits were dealt with, the pack investigated. They found some clues and with a combination of allies and contacts, plus talking to local spirits, they concluded that a man (he was claimed, they just didnt know that yet) used some water magics (Influence) to back up sewage in the area (he was testing his new powers). A little more contact use and they knew where the man was staying.<br /> -They performed the sacred hunt rite, declaring the &quot;man&quot; as their target, with the goal of ending his &quot;spreading of misery&quot;.<br /> -They went to the hotel he was staying, they distracted the front desk clerk and made a keycard to his room.<br /> -Inside his room they investigated some more. With various clues (newspaper clippings, pamphlets, etc) they concluded he was very interested in a nearby inlet, and that was likely his next target (they are in a coastal city).<br /> -They split up, two uratha started tracking him, from the hotel (in case they were wrong) and the other four went straight to the inlet. He was there, so they got the other two to conclude the hunt.<br /> -There was a battle, one claimed (rank 2 spirit inside the guy) an four rank 1 water spirits. He had the dread powers of armor 1 and claws 2 (the damaging one, I don't recall its name) as well as his influence. It was tougher than the misery spirits, due to his higher defense, damage output, and water making it more difficult to get a solid hit in. But overall it was still fairly easy. Only two players even took gauru. And at the end I believe the most damage anyone had was 3 lethal. (Which would be different if we were playing Hunter or Changeling, but this is Werewolf, that's just a scratch) They concluded the hunt.<br /> <br /> So overall their trek hasn't been that difficult or hard. So no one believes they've &quot;earned&quot; glory and they want to go find something &quot;glorious&quot; to fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487042#post487042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned this in the other thread, but in order to avoid this issue, I first find out what my players are interested in buying next, and then plan for that in the chronicle. So, two players tell me they both want to buy a dot of Glory. Cool. I know that Renown dots cost 3 experiences, and I know my players earn an average of 4 Beats per session. At that rate, they'll have enough to buy that dot of Glory in about 4 sessions. So, I plan an opportunity for them to do something Glorious, and prepare a 4 session questline culminating in that event. If they get up to 3 xp a little early, that's fine, they have a bit of a head start on what ever they want to pursue next. If they're still a few Beats short by the time they do the Glorious thing, that's fine too, I'll just note that they're a few Beats in debt.<br /> <br /> In general, my games are very player-directed. At the most basic level, they set the goals, and I put obstacles in the way of those goals. If possible, I try to do it in a way that poses dramatic questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you're saying and our group doesn't work that way. I've tried in the past, but we have a mix of very &quot;self-driven&quot; players and &quot;I just want to follow what's happening&quot; players. The self driven players always have goals, ideas, things they want to do. But then they also live in fear of stealing the spotlight from everyone constantly. The other players don't know what they want to do, but they know it isn't just follow the self driven characters around on personal goals.<br /> We've found a healthy way to deal with it, and that is to have a chronicle &quot;direction&quot; or &quot;stated goal.&quot; An underlying theme, if you will. And I, as storyteller, craft situations or stories that line up with that. So if our theme was &quot;protect your territory from outside incursions&quot; the players want those outside incursions. So they're afraid if they decide to &quot;chase down something glorious to fight&quot; then it would distract from the &quot;protecting territory&quot; theme and make the &quot;follow what's happening&quot; players sad.<br /> <br /> Also, my players are really, really, <i>really</i>, bad at deciding ahead of time what they want to spend xp on. So in your example, those two players would tell me they want to buy a dot of Glory and they have the xp right now. The only &quot;saving&quot; xp they do is because they can't decide between two merits that both cost 1xp, then suddenly they have 2xp, so lets go buy a dot of brawl.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, is four the average for most games? This is also the first chronicle we've been using the beats system (we weren't going to switch in the middle and this is our first since GM update came out) and it seems like people are getting more than that. 1 just for showing up. They generally hit 2-3 aspirations every session. Plus the totem aspiration. They always take a dramatic failure (maybe I'm not making them dramatic enough?) and quite often get one for exceptional success in pursuit of the sacred hunt. Most players are getting 6 or more fairly regularly. Is that weird?<br /> <br /> Thanks again!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T23:17:34-07:00","id":487065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487060#post487060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside, is four the average for most games? This is also the first chronicle we've been using the beats system (we weren't going to switch in the middle and this is our first since GM update came out) and it seems like people are getting more than that. 1 just for showing up. They generally hit 2-3 aspirations every session. Plus the totem aspiration. They always take a dramatic failure (maybe I'm not making them dramatic enough?) and quite often get one for exceptional success in pursuit of the sacred hunt. Most players are getting 6 or more fairly regularly. Is that weird?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's actually my group that's slow at gaining Beats. It's not their fault, I use a homebrewed hybrid system that includes both personal and group Beats, which slows down individual progress a bit, but keeps the group advancing at a similar pace. Specifically, I add a group Beat pool. Instead of everyone gaining 1 Beat for showing up, I put 1 Beat in the group pool each session. I also have the group come up with a single Group Aspiration (I started doing this in my vampire game, but for Werewolf I'd replace this with the Totem Aspiration), and whenever they complete it I put 1 Beat in the group pool. When the group pool hits 5, everyone gets 1 Experience. Character Aspirations, Conditions, and Dramatic Failures still all award individual Beats, and my players usually get around 3 or 4 of these per session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T23:19:44-07:00","id":487066,"title":"","content":"I haven't ran Werewolf under 2nd edition yet, but, in first edition, the cost of Reknown was generally so high that by the time PC's had the xp to buy the reknown, they'd accomplished something that they could hold up and claim as the justification for that reknown purchase. <br /> <br /> I haven't seen how 2nd edition xp flows yet though so... that might not be a thing. <br /> <br /> I would not recommend handing out Reknown. You run the risk of massively powerful PC's sitting on huge reserves of xp that they don't have to spend because reknown is free. <br /> That said, experimentation can be fun. If you and your group like to experiment, it might be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5514-qcks","name":"Qcks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T23:42:36-07:00","id":487072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Qcks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487066#post487066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen how 2nd edition xp flows yet though so... that might not be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Costs are flattened and affinity Renown no longer has a differentiated cost or cap and runs at an even fifteen Beats per dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T23:44:19-07:00","id":487073,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest a couple things:<br /> <br /> 1) Lower the bar for what's glorious enough. Any Werewolf interested in getting 1 dot in a Renown should be able to do it with only a smidgen of effort. The accomplishment isn't really huge; it's like a teenager getting their driver's license. It's a milestone from the perspective of &quot;you're the protagonist and growing up&quot;, but to society at large, it's mostly worth a pat on the back. Renown 1 is something cool to your family. Renown 2 is something cool to your neighborhood. All the neighbors say, &quot;Oh, and that's Sam, who's attending John Hopkins.&quot; That kind of thing.<br /> <br /> 2) Diversify what you consider glorious. It doesn't have to be a fight; it just has to be a story worth telling. Pull ahead of your packmaates while chasing something down and do something crazy to make yourself stand out. Pull <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hacks_at_the_Massachusetts_Institute_of_Technology\" target=\"_blank\">an MIT prank</a>. Resolve a confrontation by singing your heart out and getting through that way. Make someone feel special. The point of Glory is being the hero of the story, but heroism takes many, many, many forms.<br /> <br /> 3) I swear I had a three but I forgot it.<br /> <br /> I'd honestly say that any exceptional success qualifies as Renown 1 if you can explain how it fits. Get the packmates in on it: have them come up with ways to talk up the accomplishment, to explain why it's was a big deal. Part of the challenge of Renown is that you have to justify it. You can either justify it by going out and finding something, or you can justify it by looking back and recognizing the significance of what you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T00:15:55-07:00","id":487077,"title":"","content":"The thing about Renown is that it isn't fame, it's a meritocratic phenomena of the People. A werewolf has to have actually done these things to justify the expenditure <i>and</i> to have the actual Experience to spend. They can't just lie or stage a publicity campaign and get a free Gift in the process. In purely meta terms, any PC contemplating a dot in a Renown has already earned it, they just haven't justified it.<br /> <br /> The cool thing is that your players are taking the questions of the Renown system and driving the story themselves. That's great, because they're telling you what they want, and they are prompting discussion of what qualifies as Glory, and <i>failing their own standards</i>. To me, that says to trust their judgment on Renown; they aren't gaming the system, and they're looking for most satisfactory means for themselves to meet the system's guidelines.<br /> <br /> I'd also say not to worry about the narrative getting too far off course. The Wolf Must Hunt, so finding Glorious prey is a matter of planning, not distraction. Likewise, if you're worried that protecting the territory is going to get lost in the narrative, then something moves in on the territory when they get lax. A Wolf-blooded gets torn to bits or addicted to a strange red drink that comes in vials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T00:17:32-07:00","id":487078,"title":"","content":"I'm playtesting Renown Beats. Every time you do something worthwhile of fitting into a renown category, you gain a beat for that category. As you grow more advanced in renown, you'll have to do more impressive things to earn beats. Not sure yet how it'll flow with XP, but so far the group's been happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T00:32:22-07:00","id":487079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487073#post487073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd suggest a couple things:<br /> <br /> 1) Lower the bar for what's glorious enough. Any Werewolf interested in getting 1 dot in a Renown should be able to do it with only a smidgen of effort. The accomplishment isn't really huge; it's like a teenager getting their driver's license. It's a milestone from the perspective of &quot;you're the protagonist and growing up&quot;, but to society at large, it's mostly worth a pat on the back. Renown 1 is something cool to your family. Renown 2 is something cool to your neighborhood. All the neighbors say, &quot;Oh, and that's Sam, who's attending John Hopkins.&quot; That kind of thing.<br /> .....</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't respond on a lot right now, busy heading to work, but I noticed that I need to clarify one thing, this isn't the <i>first</i> dot of renown these characters are seeking.<br /> For one character, it's the <i>second</i> dot of Glory. For the other, the <i>third.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T02:37:17-07:00","id":487131,"title":"","content":"Haven't read 2nd ed yet, so Beats are beyond me.<br /> <br /> 1st ed had a few examples of feats for each specific Renown. If 2nd ed has the same things, you can offer them as examples for the players.<br /> <br /> I've found that instead of telling the players what they need to do to earn Renown, it's best I just drive on with the story, and at the end of the session(or at home) I'll go through the feats of Renown, see if the players have performed any and note down what Renown they're eligible to buy when they have enough XP.<br /> <br /> If you're doing this and the players know what to aim for, your players will soon have no trouble getting some Glory.<br /> <br /> Also, as someone above suggested, lower the expectations for renown, even down to a few hard rolls if possible (after they've role-played intensively of course).<br /> <br /> As for increasingly harder feats required for higher renown, why bother with that headache? You've got 6 players already, that should be headache enough. Just rule that feats of Renown are cumulative, with many small stories of glory adding ONE BIG GLORY RENOWN. As a possible variation of this, a particularly notable glorious feat nets the player/players eligibility for two dots of the Glory Renown.<br /> <br /> If you've implemented any of this and are worried about an explosion of renown, just make it more expensive to buy XP-wise.<br /> <br /> One man's opinion, folks. Don't bite my head off. Skull is hard to chew anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":2603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","user":"iamthenight","date":". 04-21-2015, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T08:53:06-07:00","id":487307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487079#post487079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't respond on a lot right now, busy heading to work, but I noticed that I need to clarify one thing, this isn't the <i>first</i> dot of renown these characters are seeking.<br /> For one character, it's the <i>second</i> dot of Glory. For the other, the <i>third.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be really helpful to hear what the characters did for their first (and second) dots of Glory. Taking down a Claimed surrounded by a cadre of attending spirits might not have been too hard for your group, but its still a reasonably impressive feat. The end damage toll to your pack may have taken less than an hour to clear out, but they might well have saved the town (and thus, their territory).<br /> The main issue in increasing Renown is that your significant action be a bigger deal than the one before it. Is the defeat of a Claimed and the saving of their city a bigger deal than what they did? Then the Renown could well be theirs. If not, then have something bigger and scarier stalk into town next time. It sounds like the chalenges you've thrown at them so far have been somewhat minor, so ramping things up a bit might not be a bad plan in general.<br /> <br /> Edit: It might not be a bad idea to, on top of having your players tell you what they did to earn the dots they already have, ask your players for their thoughts on what actions might be worth the new dots. My character, for example, got his first Wisdom for supplicating a Lune. His second was for helping create a Fettish. His third was for discovering (if not recording and keeping) a lost Rite. I think leading the creation of a 4-dot Fettish would be worth the fourth (or maybe a 3-dot one depending on the circumstances) and supplicating a major spirit (like Death Wolf or Luna herself) for something would be worth the fifth.<br /> <br /> You mentioned that they don't feel like they've done something Glorious enough. Find out what they would see as sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 04-21-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T10:33:48-07:00","id":487425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487131#post487131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for increasingly harder feats required for higher renown, why bother with that headache?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty explicit in the 2e corebook. The &quot;Increasing Renown&quot; section comes down to two things: each successive dot requires topping yourself; actually getting the dot is mostly about persuading the Lunes to agree that you deserve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T15:00:21-07:00","id":487677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487425#post487425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty explicit in the 2e corebook. The &quot;Increasing Renown&quot; section comes down to two things: each successive dot requires topping yourself; actually getting the dot is mostly about persuading the Lunes to agree that you deserve.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we're referencing rules, here's one from the nWoD Corebook.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Story First, Rules Second: </b>Rules are tools. Use them, but don't let them trap you. If you make the odd change here or there to encourage the flow of the story, no one will notice (or at least care).</i><br /> <br /> Everyone seems to conveniently forget that one for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T15:19:09-07:00","id":487687,"title":"","content":"I figure if someone has done something worthy of a second dot <i>and</i> something worthy of a third, it shouldn't matter if they did them in the wrong order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T16:55:37-07:00","id":487798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487677#post487677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're referencing rules, here's one from the nWoD Corebook.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Story First, Rules Second: </b>Rules are tools. Use them, but don't let them trap you. If you make the odd change here or there to encourage the flow of the story, no one will notice (or at least care).</i><br /> <br /> Everyone seems to conveniently forget that one for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the quote from the section Errol216 is referencing is not really a rule, so much as it is fluff text. Specifically, it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Uratha might, soon after his First Change, undertake massive efforts to impress his peers. Many young Forsaken die less than a year after the First Change in efforts to impress their new families. Sometimes, success results in downright epic accomplishments that shower a young werewolf with Renown. The problem is, a character sets her own bar for Renown. With every increase, she raises that bar. To go further, she must improve upon her previous achievements. Some Uratha accomplish themselves into a proverbial corner this way; They do something so remarkable that they can\u2019t hope to do better. </div> </div> </div>It's specifically <i>because</i> of &quot;Story First, Rules Second&quot; that the above quote should influence what justification the ST requires of the players in order to earn their Renown purchases, since by actual RAW you can spend experiences on whatever you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T19:19:40-07:00","id":487851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487677#post487677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While we're referencing rules, here's one from the nWoD Corebook.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Story First, Rules Second: </b>Rules are tools. Use them, but don't let them trap you. If you make the odd change here or there to encourage the flow of the story, no one will notice (or at least care).</i><br /> <br /> Everyone seems to conveniently forget that one for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>If my aid is not welcome, you do not need to insult me in return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T21:26:38-07:00","id":487951,"title":"","content":"Thanks, everyone, for such helpful replies and advice. I always love that I can turn to these boards and get so much help.<br /> <br /> You guys have given me quite a bit to think about and I'm going to go through everything and talk with my group, we'll find something that works.<br /> <br /> Someone asked about what the group had already done to gain their previous dots, unfortunately we don't know. We really need to discuss that and come up with the stories this pack has already done, but everyone was really excited to play, this form of character creation was truly different and marvelous (making the whole pack), especially with the amount of &quot;togetherness&quot; and such that we haven't had in our games in a long time. We spent two weeks on &quot;session 0's&quot; coming up with everything, I didn't want to nitpick about the few things that got glossed over. And maybe that was a mistake, but it's one we're trying to rectify as we play along.<br /> <br /> One thing that I don't think got answered too much, one player did suggest that we treat renown completely as a story reward and not use xp on it at all. I think a couple people touched on that (one saying use &quot;renown beats&quot; and one saying that would create loads of &quot;leftover xp&quot; if I recall correctly). But I think it is an idea worth investigating at least. Has anyone else done this? Do you think having a lot of xp &quot;freed up&quot; because you don't have to spend it on renown would cause much of an issue? Would you still give the free facet with the dot as well, or make them go ahead and buy that, just using renown as an extra &quot;supernatural attribute&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T01:05:41-07:00","id":488049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487798#post487798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The problem is, a character sets her own bar for Renown. </span></i></span></span></b></u><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">With every increase, <u><b>she </b></u>raises that bar. To go further, <b><u>she</u> </b>must improve upon her previous achievements. <u><b>Some Uratha accomplish themselves into a proverbial corner this way; </b></u>They do something so remarkable that they can\u2019t hope to do better.</span></i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Fluff references an individual and/or a small group, not Uratha as a whole. Conceivably, since <u>some characters</u> do this, most have figured out it's not smart to do this, ergo, my small-deeds-one-big-renown approach is still perfectly valid. And even if this wasn't the case, the fluff itself isn't a holy text. The story is put together by the storyteller and the players, not the fluff in the manual. That's just a helper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":2603,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","user":"iamthenight","date":". 04-22-2015, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T05:20:34-07:00","id":488181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487951#post487951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone asked about what the group had already done to gain their previous dots, unfortunately we don't know. We really need to discuss that and come up with the stories this pack has already done, but everyone was really excited to play, this form of character creation was truly different and marvelous (making the whole pack), especially with the amount of &amp;quot;togetherness&amp;quot; and such that we haven't had in our games in a long time. We spent two weeks on &amp;quot;session 0's&amp;quot; coming up with everything, I didn't want to nitpick about the few things that got glossed over. And maybe that was a mistake, but it's one we're trying to rectify as we play along.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my thought. And I get what you're saying about wanting to really get rolling with the game after two sessions of character creation. Luckily, if you have your players' contact information, this is not something you need to do on game night. Let your players know that it would be helpful to know what they've done and what they think would be appropriate for Renown gains and have them email you their thoughts. That way, you'll get both the story and the game time that's dedicated to playing.<br /> <br /> @iamthenight: The point of this fluff is to be a massive plot hook. You fell from orbit to get your most recent Glory dot? Well think of something super sweet for your next one. Then you get to DO that thing that's more Glorious than surviving a fall from orbit. How cool is that? It just takes a little bit of cooperation between the GM and the players. It also requires the players jumping on the chance when they see it, but that's what makes the stories good.<br /> That said, there definitely is room for your slow-bleed-of-Renown idea. There was a thread at one point asking about how to raise Purity, pointing out that the &quot;take a human mate&quot; suggestion seemed like it could never be good for much other than the first or maybe second dot. My counterpoint to that was that, if your character had dutifully held to every other tenant of the Oath of the Moon other than &quot;Wolf shall cleave to Human&quot;, taking a human mate could mean bringing your Purity to a sense of completion and fullness, thereby warranting the fifth dot.<br /> In this schema, you'd think of the first dot as &quot;oh, I get this concept&quot;, the second as &quot;I have done serious work with this concept&quot;, the second as &quot;This concept is something I'm good at&quot;, the fourth as &quot;I am an exemplar of this concept&quot;, and the fifth as &quot;This concept is a rule of life for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yes, story before rules. Stop and think how the rules could enhance the story before you throw them out, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T09:07:14-07:00","id":488357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=488049#post488049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fluff references an individual and/or a small group, not Uratha as a whole. Conceivably, since <u>some characters</u> do this, most have figured out it's not smart to do this, ergo, my small-deeds-one-big-renown approach is still perfectly valid. And even if this wasn't the case, the fluff itself isn't a holy text. The story is put together by the storyteller and the players, not the fluff in the manual. That's just a helper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'm not saying you're forced to follow what it says, Just that &quot;story first, rules second&quot; is not a counter-argument to &quot;the narrative text says Renown requires increasingly impressive feats to earn.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:16:04-07:00","id":488704,"title":"","content":"@Tiarn: If a Renown dot awards you a Gift as it did in 1st edition, I'd recommend asking them to spend XP. Otherwise they might end up solely going after feats of Renown to get free gift, which might unbalance your game if you can't compensate, though it's perfectly alright if you <i>can </i>compensate for it.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't reward a Gift, by all means, go full story! Less hassle for both you and your players.<br /> <br /> That being said, here are the 1st ed Feats of Renown. Not sure if this is legal or not, but I've seen others quoting stuff directly, so here goes.<br /> <br /> Feats of Cunning: Killing a foe and making his allies believe the death was accidental; convincing one foe to attack another; avoiding potential human discovery of the Uratha without the use of violence; a new and original battle strategy; any monumental act of stealth, manipulation, cleverness or diplomacy.<br /> <br /> Feats of Glory: Winning a battle or outmaneuvering a foe in a spectacular or especially triumphant way; winning a battle in the name of a lover, ancestor or totem; telling an epic story that is later repeated by others; telling a stirring rendition of a traditional tale; acting as inspiration to fellow Forsaken; any other monumental feat of bravery, tradition, valor or daring.<br /> <br /> Feats of Honor: Adjudicating a fair challenge between other werewolves; performing one\u2019s duties to the pack and totem in the face of extreme adversity; participating in a just challenge; uncovering taint or injustice; striking a diplomatic truce with a potent rival spirit; any monumental feat of justice, truth or fairness.<br /> <br /> Feats of Purity: Leading a righteous crusade against enemies of Luna and the People; slaying a true foe in proper combat; saving the lives of other werewolves or the wolf-blooded; remaining true to the Oath even when tempted or coerced to do otherwise; any other feat of monumental self-restraint, zeal or morality (as expressed via Harmony).<br /> <br /> Feats of Wisdom: Solving a great spiritual riddle; developing a new rite; binding a potent spirit; discovering and exploiting an enemy spirit\u2019s ban; creating or strengthening<br /> a locus; negotiating a suitable compromise; any monumental act of logic, intelligence, memory or intuition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> @TerraBen: Please reread my original post, since I've already answered that falling from orbit issue. I'm sure any ST worth his salt can extrapolate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487131#post487131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't read 2nd ed yet, so Beats are beyond me.<br /> <br /> 1st ed had a few examples of feats for each specific Renown. If 2nd ed has the same things, you can offer them as examples for the players.<br /> <br /> I've found that instead of telling the players what they need to do to earn Renown, it's best I just drive on with the story, and at the end of the session(or at home) I'll go through the feats of Renown, see if the players have performed any and note down what Renown they're eligible to buy when they have enough XP.<br /> <br /> If you're doing this and the players know what to aim for, your players will soon have no trouble getting some Glory.<br /> <br /> Also, as someone above suggested, lower the expectations for renown, even down to a few hard rolls if possible (after they've role-played intensively of course).<br /> <br /> As for increasingly harder feats required for higher renown, why bother with that headache? You've got 6 players already, that should be headache enough. Just rule that feats of Renown are cumulative, with many small stories of glory adding ONE BIG GLORY RENOWN. <u><b>As a possible variation of this, a particularly notable glorious feat nets the player/players eligibility for two dots of the Glory Renown.</b></u><br /> <br /> If you've implemented any of this and are worried about an explosion of renown, just make it more expensive to buy XP-wise.<br /> <br /> One man's opinion, folks. Don't bite my head off. Skull is hard to chew anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> @Charlaquin: I only used it to combat a rule lawyer's reference of a rule which turned out to be a fluff. The rule/fluff confusion was his, not mine.<br /> <br /> To be honest, it's the only &quot;rule&quot;(metarule, really!) I ever use nowadays. My games are quite different from the basic RAW, even fluff-wise. I no longer see the point of being stuck in a rule/fluff cage, and my players are fine with that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:30:51-07:00","id":488722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=488704#post488704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, it's the only &quot;rule&quot;(metarule, really!) I ever use nowadays. My games are quite different from the basic RAW, even fluff-wise. <b>I no longer see the point of being stuck in a rule/fluff cage, and my players are fine with that.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone whose gradual concentrated readthrough of the entire nWoD has come with an increasing lack of exactingness when it comes to the mechanics, I must implore you to be aware that other people are not you and that the existence of adhered-to structure in their games ought not be a personal affront to your sensibilities.<br /> <br /> The other forumgoers are not your players, this place is not your blog, and &quot;you can discard rules if they don't suit the needs or fancies of your table&quot; is not a thing that it is useful to say outside the context of overbearing insistence that the rules supersede all else.<br /> <br /> Kindly lay off of Errol and stick to helpful behavior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:41:36-07:00","id":488729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>iamthenight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=487677#post487677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While we're referencing rules, here's one from the nWoD Corebook.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Story First, Rules Second: </b>Rules are tools. Use them, but don't let them trap you. If you make the odd change here or there to encourage the flow of the story, no one will notice (or at least care).</i><br /> <br /> Everyone seems to conveniently forget that one for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understanding the how and why of the mechanics(Even 'fluff' mechanics, such as the subject here) and the reasoning behind them allows us to meaningfully determine the how and why of deviations we take away from them, leading to a more coherent and cohesive storytelling/gaming experience.<br /> <br /> If we always arbitrarily put story first, we negate the purpose to having rules in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-22-2015, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:49:37-07:00","id":488804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=488722#post488722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;you can discard rules if they don't suit the needs or fancies of your table&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=488729#post488729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we always arbitrarily put story first, we negate the purpose to having rules in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely on the dot. My hope is that one day the role-players of the world will understand the uselessness of the rule/fluff cage. Until then, however, I'm afraid my words are falling of deaf ears.<br /> <br /> Apologies if my arguments have offended the local rules lawyers.<br /> <br /> Tiarn, hope I've helped a bit, and best of luck with your campaign.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://multiversalmoments.weebly.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2603-iamthenight","name":"iamthenight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:38:08-07:00","id":488826,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Let's all refrain from namecalling and insulting other players' preferred styles, please.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T11:25:18-07:00","id":492749,"title":"","content":"So with renown we no longer need to increase auspice renown first yes? It's free form now? And soon as you have 4 dots you're effectivly rank 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T18:44:39-07:00","id":493111,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Auspice Renown no longer caps the other Renowns and, unless you're a Ghost Wolf, your first in-game Renown increase makes your effective Rank 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:00:20-07:00","id":493126,"title":"","content":"Sucks for ghost wolves. Still better then milk toast in bloodborne","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:17:41-07:00","id":493138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=493126#post493126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sucks for ghost wolves. Still better then milk toast in bloodborne</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to derail the thread to pursue a passing reference, but...<br /> <br /> milk... toast...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:50:33-07:00","id":493171,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://dictionary.reference.com/browse/Milquetoast%20?s=t\" target=\"_blank\">Milquetoast</a>. In the game it looks like all your stats start as average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T05:20:07-07:00","id":493474,"title":"","content":"Just like the commoner or peasant or whatever they were called in the previous Demon's Souls, Dark Souls 1+2 games, that class can be amazing if you've got a build in mind, since it doesn't start with any &quot;misplaced&quot; stat points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T18:23:38-07:00","id":494187,"title":"","content":"It also has the description of being worthless and states you should have never been born. Which sometimes fits into the derogatory way ghost Wolves are stared at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T19:42:19-07:00","id":494246,"title":"","content":"Ok, got it. As a point of clarification, the Milquetoast Origin gives average stats in everything but has the same total points as all the other backgrounds, and it's just describes your character as having a &quot;normal&quot;, uneventful upbringing. It's the <i>Waste of Skin Origin</i> that has the lower stat total than all the others and describes your character as worthless and should never have been born. (I had to look that up, since I haven't gotten around to buying Bloodborne yet, hence my initial confusion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T20:55:59-07:00","id":494336,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah no it's definently a gimped set compared to the others, but you have room to grow how you want (als ghost wolves)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T13:22:00-07:00","id":495122,"title":"","content":"On-topic, I'd say if your characters want to increase their Renown, thats a really good Aspiration to chase up, if worded in whatever way you wish your character to achieve it. I won't bother listing example Aspirations, though these will get you them awesome Beats that build up into Experience with which to buy the Renown boost. Because your Aspirations have been looking to build that up specifically going in, there should be more than enough reasons through past sessions to net it story-wise.<br /> I know it's been stated that there are players out there that may want to get Renown on a whim because they just so happen to have the xp, though again I'd say to look back at where they achieved their Beats. I think for things like that, taking notes or having a character diary can really help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T19:54:55-07:00","id":497012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/487011-raising-renown?p=495122#post495122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On-topic, I'd say if your characters want to increase their Renown, thats a really good Aspiration to chase up, if worded in whatever way you wish your character to achieve it. I won't bother listing example Aspirations, though these will get you them awesome Beats that build up into Experience with which to buy the Renown boost. Because your Aspirations have been looking to build that up specifically going in, there should be more than enough reasons through past sessions to net it story-wise.<br /> I know it's been stated that there are players out there that may want to get Renown on a whim because they just so happen to have the xp, though again I'd say to look back at where they achieved their Beats. I think for things like that, taking notes or having a character diary can really help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I's second this - looking for specific Renown is looking for sepecific actions - and this could easily work as Aspirations. The in-setting look on Renowns is they make you more powerfull, so our characters can literally look for actions of Glory, Honor or Purity. And making it long term is great way for characters to generate cool scenes! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have also advise this after mine short run with 1ed Renowns - <b>if main plot of the group do not let the PCs to &quot;earn&quot; their Renowns in spotlight - just let them in the backlight.</b> When characters are waiting, few days past between scenes or some other event interupets normal flow of session - just let player to describe what his charater achive when buying the Renown by the Expieirnace <i>he still collected before</i>. Player earned the right to get Renown by collecting the Beats for it early, he just need the &quot;excuse&quot; for raising the trait. And imaginig this reason is enougth for taking it - like with the idea of asking Lunes for the dot of Wisdom. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even if other PCs could not be with character in question on scene, they can easily hear later on this deed, even from spirits - this &quot;fame&quot; in Uratha and spirits society is what Renown is all about.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> <i>Mark has Irraka character. On last few game sessions he wanted to rise his Cunning Renown to third dot. He even made an Aspiration of it for his PC. He got few Beats from it and collected all others from other sources. Sadly, no good scene errupted to earn him the Renown dot buy. But the plot of the chronicle is in-stale for 3 days, as the pack is prepering for their next big Sacred Hunt. Mark has now in-game time for his PC to earn his Cunning. He descirbes how his Irraka is tricked their neighboors pack in to getting them Loci they all wanted. Mark spend Experiance on the Cunning dot and rest of his pack can spend on buying new Loci as Merit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i><br /> <br /> With player doing a job of thinking for the cool scene on his own and maybe creating other favroable conditions for others by this - I think it's cool solution for the problem of rising Renown when normal plot do not lend you to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T22:07:56-07:00","id":497093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>if main plot of the group do not let the PCs to &quot;earn&quot; their Renowns in spotlight - just let them in the backlight.</b> </div> </div> </div>Always an option. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though seeing as it takes 15 Beats to make up one point of Renown, there are gonna be examples of actions your characters have done to have got them. I've noticed in upgrading my own Uratha that they naturally become more 3D as you go and going from a concept to a full character really shows where they excel at and what they could do for Aspirations... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T04:09:33-07:00","id":497302,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Ham. That was a really good write up! I like your example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}